-- title:
--   Candidate ledgers and actual prediction parameters
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. An ordered tree has finite levels $0,1,2,\dots$ with a single root, and monotone surjective parent maps from level $k+1$ to level $k$; edge weights are positive and sum to $1$ over the children of each parent. Each node carries a nonexpansive selfmap of $K$, and the tree is evaluated bottom-up: a node's value is its map applied to the weighted average of its children's values. Fix an ordered tree, a level $k$, and a set $Y$ of stored points.
--
--   1. **Ledger.** All candidates of the level, retained or discarded: their number, a monotone parent map to level $k$, their points, and an order embedding of the level-$(k+1)$ nodes into the candidates that preserves parents.
--   2. **Coefficients.** Retained candidates get their tree weight, discarded ones get $0$. Every parent group has total coefficient $1$.
--   3. **Earlier candidates.** For a node $v$, all candidates strictly before its own (including discarded ones), with their parents and points.
--   4. **Actual parameter.** $\theta_v$, the coefficients restricted to the earlier candidates. It lies in the coefficient set, and the ideal child average equals the residual point:
--   $$
--   \sum_{\mathrm{par}(w)=p}w_kw\cdot\mathrm{val}(w)=r_p(\theta_v)
--   $$
--   when retained children before $v$ carry their values and the others carry the base point $b$.
